Description: install, secure and run a small network fabric
 fabricctl sets up and manages fabric on this host: authoritative DNS
 (BIND9) with RFC2136/TSIG, an internal PKI (Step-CA), secrets (OpenBao),
 389 Directory Server, Keycloak SSO and the Open Fabric web UI behind
 client certificates and OIDC; optionally Kea DHCP, 802.1X (FreeRADIUS)
 and log forwarding (Fluent Bit) — every service in a hardened container
 under systemd (fabric.target). Installing the package changes nothing; run
 `sudo fabricctl setup` to install fabric.

